Build an API Reference with OpenAPI and Swagger UI
Objectives
Author an OpenAPI 3.0 YAML specification for a sample task-tracker API
Document endpoints with parameters, request/response schemas, and API key authentication
Serve and test the spec interactively using Swagger UI on a local Linux machine
Export the rendered documentation as a static HTML site
Prerequisites
Basic familiarity with REST API concepts (endpoints, HTTP methods, JSON)
Comfortable with Linux terminal and a text editor (nano/vim)
Basic YAML syntax knowledge
No prior Swagger/OpenAPI experience required, but helpful
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine via Start Lab — use it for all steps below
Verify internet access for package installation
sudo apt update
node -v || curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo -E bash -
sudo apt install -y nodejs
node -v && npm -v
Create a working directory:
mkdir -p ~/api-docs-lab && cd ~/api-docs-lab
